WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:04.910
49. The Shakespeare of Rock and Roll.

2
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:13.180
In 2016, a songwriter won the Nobel Prize in Literature for the first time.

3
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:19.180
But this is only the latest victory for the man often called the greatest American poet of the 20th century.

4
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.180
Ladies and gentlemen, meet Bob Dylan.

5
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:32.180
Born in Minnesota in 1941, Robert Zimmerman changed his name and moved to New York in 1961 to make a career in music.

6
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:38.180
Originally a folk singer, he played social and political songs in coffee shops for small crowds.

7
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:45.180
He was soon noticed by Columbia Records, and his first album, Bob Dylan, was released in 1962.

8
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:51.180
Although his early records weren't very big sellers, Dylan quickly found success as a songwriter.

9
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:58.180
His famous protest song, Blowing in the Wind, was a hit for the folk trio Peter, Paul and Mary in 1963.

10
00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:03.180
Since then, countless other artists have covered Dylan's songs.

11
00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:09.180
In 1965, Dylan shocked the music world by switching from soft folk to hard rock.

12
00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:14.180
While some of his old fans were disappointed, many new fans were created.

13
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:20.180
The single, like a rolling stone, reached number two in the United States, making Dylan a star.

14
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.180
A couple of years later, he changed styles again, writing and playing quiet country songs.

15
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:30.180
Now the rock fans were upset, but Dylan just kept moving forward.

16
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:35.180
1969's Nashville Skyline was as fast as selling album yet.

17
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.180
The end of the 1960s did not bring an end to Dylan's success.

18
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.180
Hits such as Knockin' on Heaven's Door, 1973, kept him in the public eye,

19
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:49.180
and 1975's Blood on the Tracks remains his best-selling album.

20
00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:54.180
More than 40 years later, he continues to record and perform around the world.

21
00:01:54.180 --> 00:02:00.180
In addition to his Nobel Prize, Dylan has won 12 Grammy Awards, an Academy Award,

22
00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.180
and the U.S. Presidential Medal of Freedom.

23
00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:09.180
The man who began his career by attacking the establishment is now very well established.
